From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: burakgon <burakgon12@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:09:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] displayid2: don't read past the section after an
 oversized data block

parse_data_block() returned the declared length of a data block that
does not fit in the remaining section. The caller then advanced past the
end of the section and checked the padding at that position with the
remaining length of the previous iteration, reading beyond the EDID
buffer. A checksum-valid EDID with one oversized DisplayID v2 data block
is enough to trigger it (AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow READ).

Consume the rest of the section instead, and compute the padding length
from the final position. Also print the size_t block length with %zu.

The jdi-lpm135m467-edp test expected a "Padding: Contains non-zero bytes"
failure that edid-decode does not report: it was this bug reading the
section checksum as padding. Update the expected diff.
---
 displayid2.c                      |  8 ++++++--
 test/data/jdi-lpm135m467-edp.diff | 11 +++++------
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/displayid2.c b/displayid2.c
index 6ab9c7b..75dd45a 100644
--- a/displayid2.c
+++ b/displayid2.c
@@ -92,9 +92,11 @@ parse_data_block(struct di_displayid2 *displayid2, const uint8_t *data,
 	data_block_size = (size_t) data[0x02] + DISPLAYID2_DATA_BLOCK_HEADER_SIZE;
 	if (data_block_size > size) {
 		add_failure(displayid2,
-			    "The length of this DisplayID data block (%d) exceeds the number of bytes remaining (%zu)",
+			    "The length of this DisplayID data block (%zu) exceeds the number of bytes remaining (%zu)",
 			    data_block_size, size);
-		goto skip;
+		/* Consume what is left of the section: the declared length
+		 * would move the caller past the end of the section. */
+		return (ssize_t) size;
 	}
 
 	data_block = calloc(1, sizeof(*data_block));
@@ -245,6 +247,8 @@ _di_displayid2_parse(struct di_displayid2 *displayid2, const uint8_t *data,
 		assert(data_block_size > 0);
 		i += (size_t) data_block_size;
 	}
+	/* Only the bytes between i and the checksum are padding. */
+	max_data_block_size = i < section_size - 1 ? section_size - 1 - i : 0;
 	if (!is_all_zeroes(&data[i], max_data_block_size)) {
 		if (max_data_block_size < DISPLAYID2_DATA_BLOCK_HEADER_SIZE) {
 			add_failure(displayid2,
diff --git a/test/data/jdi-lpm135m467-edp.diff b/test/data/jdi-lpm135m467-edp.diff
index c5167a0..c6b3f3c 100644
--- a/test/data/jdi-lpm135m467-edp.diff
+++ b/test/data/jdi-lpm135m467-edp.diff
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 --- ref
 +++ di
-@@ -36,32 +36,13 @@
+@@ -36,32 +36,9 @@
  
  Block 1, DisplayID Extension Block:
    Version: 2.0
@@ -22,8 +22,8 @@
 -Block 0, Base EDID:
 -  Missing Display Product Name.
 -
- Failures:
- 
+-Failures:
+-
 -Block 0, Base EDID:
 -  Alphanumeric Data String: No newline, but one or more trailing spaces.
 -  Alphanumeric Data String: No newline, but one or more trailing spaces.
@@ -33,6 +33,5 @@
 -  DisplayID: Missing DisplayID Type VII Detailed Timing Data Block.
 -  DisplayID: DisplayID expects at least one preferred timing.
 -
-+Block 1, DisplayID Extension Block:
-+  Padding: Contains non-zero bytes.
- EDID conformity: FAIL
+-EDID conformity: FAIL
++EDID conformity: PASS
